Subject: [PATCH] clkdev: accommodate AM335x interconnect device names

AM335x clock aliases include interconnect paths longer than 24 bytes.
Keep the complete device ID instead of installing an unusable "bad" alias.

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://lists.openwall.net/linux-kernel/2025/11/14/616]

--- a/drivers/clk/clkdev.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/clkdev.c
@@ -147,2 +147,2 @@
-#define MAX_DEV_ID	24
+#define MAX_DEV_ID	64
 #define MAX_CON_ID	16
